<http://data.silknow.org/actor/6461fab0-b6df-3f87-9771-989bf1ccf9d6>
        a                         ecrm:E39_Actor ;
        rdfs:label                "1914 until at least 1922, Morris and Co., London [see note 1]. January 22, anonymous (\"property of a gentleman\") sale, Christie's, London, lot 191. Acquired on the London art market by S. Franses and Co., London; 2002, sold by Franses to the MFA. (Accession Date: March 20) NOTES: [1] See Linda Parry, \"The revival of the Merton Abbey Tapestry Works,\" Journal of the William Morris Society, vol. 5, no. 3 (Summer), p. 19 and p. 22, n. 9. / Charles Potter Kling Fund" ;
        ecrm:P1_is_identified_by  "1914 until at least 1922, Morris and Co., London [see note 1]. January 22, anonymous (\"property of a gentleman\") sale, Christie's, London, lot 191. Acquired on the London art market by S. Franses and Co., London; 2002, sold by Franses to the MFA. (Accession Date: March 20) NOTES: [1] See Linda Parry, \"The revival of the Merton Abbey Tapestry Works,\" Journal of the William Morris Society, vol. 5, no. 3 (Summer), p. 19 and p. 22, n. 9. / Charles Potter Kling Fund" .

